# .gitignore — DENY-BY-DEFAULT seam enforcer (standalone-l3 dual-layer + RL4 directed visibility)
#
# Strategy: ignore EVERYTHING first, then explicitly un-ignore the classified shareable-core
# paths. Any new/unclassified path therefore defaults to PRIVATE. Classify a new path in INDEX.md
# and add an un-ignore line below before it can be tracked.
#
# RL4 note: the highest-risk PRIVATE buckets here hold identity-bearing material — raw local
# transcripts + identity-bearing analysis intermediates + the coordinate staging. They must NEVER
# be tracked. The upward coordinate carries no identity but is still operator output → PRIVATE.

# 1. Deny everything.
/*
/.*

# 2. Un-ignore shareable-core top-level files.
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/INDEX.md
!/manifest.yaml
!/.env.template
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# 3. Un-ignore shareable-core directories (then re-deny private leaves inside them).
!/decisions/
!/planning/
!/self-growth/
!/scripts/
!/.claude/
!/config/

# 3b. .claude/ is mixed: settings.json is [S]; the harness's MACHINE-LOCAL permission ledger is
#     [P] (approved-command strings land there verbatim). Never track it.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# 4. config/ is mixed: allow the templates + schema, deny the private instances.
config/*
!config/path-mappings.yaml
!config/personal-domains.yaml
!config/extraction.schema.json
!config/STATE-template.md
!config/usage-limits.template.json
!config/.gitkeep
# private config instances stay ignored (NOT un-ignored):
#   config/STATE.md
#   config/path-mappings.filled.yaml
#   config/usage-limits.json          (personal plan limits)

# 5. self-growth/ is mixed: allow mechanism + core log, deny the private log.
self-growth/*
!self-growth/insight-log-core.md
!self-growth/README.md
!self-growth/.gitkeep
# self-growth/insight-log-private.md stays ignored.

# 6. PRIVATE data buckets — never tracked (RL4: identity-bearing). NOT un-ignored:
#   raw-sessions/   — raw local transcripts + identity-bearing analysis (highest sensitivity)
#   handoff/        — coordinate uploads (the only file type that leaves, hand-carried → private)
#   output/         — personal-facing growth advice (real self-view → private)
#   worktemp/       — scratch

# 7. Python bytecode caches — noise, never tracked (scripts/ is un-ignored above, so a
#    __pycache__/ under it would otherwise be commit-eligible).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
